    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0234" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Marshall and Dr. Stuart to General
                        Chou En-lai </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-26">26 September 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear General Chou</hi>: Since your departure for
                    Shanghai we have been steadily hoping that you would return here and thus make
                    possible a resumption of the efforts to end the spreading civil war. The
                    disastrous consequences to the nation of a continuation of the present situation
                    are apparent to all. We continue in our belief that both the Government and the
                    Communist leaders sincerely desire peace and the establishment of a coalition
                    government and the adoption of a democratic constitution, and that the
                    difficulties are largely questions of procedure.</p>
                <p>We desire to help in this to the utmost of our ability. We venture, therefore, on
                    the basis of our past friendly relations and our personal esteem for you, to
                    urge that you return to Nanking without further delay in order that we may
                    together explore all conceivable ways and means for the objective we are seeking
                    to achieve.</p>
                <p>We have been informed that the Generalissimo returns to Nanking today or
                    tomorrow, weather permitting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. C. Marshall</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. L. Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
